1
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:05,790
Previously on Friends:

2
00:00:02,710 --> 00:00:05,790
I don't feel like I have a girlfriend.

3
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:09,040
You want me to quit my job so you can feel like you have a girlfriend?

4
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:11,170
Is this about Mark?

5
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:11,170
Oh, my God.

6
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:13,670
Okay, it's not.

7
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:13,670
Oh, my God.

8
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:16,050
I cannot keep having this fight with you!

9
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:18,510
Look, ugh, maybe we should just take a break.

10
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:20,850
Fine. You're right. Let's, uh, take a break.

11
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:23,930
Let's get some frozen yogurt.

12
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:23,930
No.

13
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:26,900
A break from us.

14
00:00:29,190 --> 00:00:32,740
Then we had this big fight, and I said I wanted to take a break.

15
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:34,700
I don't want to take a break.

16
00:00:34,860 --> 00:00:36,030
This is crazy.

17
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,910
Can't we work on this?

18
00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:39,160
What do you want to drink?

19
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:41,160
Who's that?

20
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,580
Nobody.

21
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:46,290
Is that Mark?

22
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:46,290
Honey, look, he just...

23
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:48,330
Yeah. Got it!

24
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:51,210
Hey, come dance. What are you, married?

25
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:54,260
Because that's okay.

26
00:01:09,270 --> 00:01:10,400
Hey.

27
00:01:09,270 --> 00:01:10,400
Hey.

28
00:01:10,570 --> 00:01:12,820
How was the big anniversary dinner?

29
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:16,030
Well, we never actually got to dinner.

30
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,950
Ha, ha, oh. Nice.

31
00:01:20,030 --> 00:01:21,830
We kind of broke up instead.

32
00:01:21,990 --> 00:01:23,660
What? Aah!

33
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:28,670
My God! It's on the ceiling!

34
00:01:28,830 --> 00:01:29,920
That's okay.

35
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:32,250
This is more important than fruit...

36
00:01:32,670 --> 00:01:34,000
...on my ceiling.

37
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:36,840
You broke up?

38
00:01:37,010 --> 00:01:40,220
Yeah, but it's okay because when Ross left, Mark came over.

39
00:01:40,390 --> 00:01:43,810
Oh, no! You and Mark?

40
00:01:40,390 --> 00:01:43,810
No, it's okay. Calm down.

41
00:01:43,970 --> 00:01:45,430
Mark and I talked...

42
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:49,850
...and I realized how much I love your stupid brother.

43
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:53,570
We got our problems, but I really wanna make it work.

44
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,040
Morning!

45
00:03:08,350 --> 00:03:10,020
Hi, it's me.

46
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:12,600
I've been trying to reach you all night. I feel awful.

47
00:03:12,770 --> 00:03:15,860
Please, Ross, you've got to know, there's nothing between me and Mark.

48
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:18,530
This whole breakup thing is just stupid.

49
00:03:21,110 --> 00:03:23,860
Ugh, I'm sorry I put you through it.

50
00:03:24,030 --> 00:03:26,620
And I don't want to get back together over a machine.

51
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,660
So I love you.

52
00:03:29,830 --> 00:03:30,870
I love you.

53
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:34,290
And you know what? I'm gonna go to bed now...

54
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:39,340
...but on my way to work tomorrow, I'll stop by around 8:30. Bye.

55
00:03:42,510 --> 00:03:43,930
Chloe, how's it coming?

56
00:03:44,090 --> 00:03:46,550
What kind of puppy do you think I should get?

57
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:48,640
Um, oh, hey. I don't know. How about a big one?

58
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:51,520
But my apartment's so...

59
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:51,520
Then a small one.

60
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:54,190
We have to go.

61
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:54,190
Wait! Where's my shoes?

62
00:03:54,350 --> 00:03:55,440
You need shoes?

63
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:02,740
Do I know why we're rushing?

64
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:02,740
You know my girlfriend?

65
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:05,990
It turns out that she, uh, wants to get back together.

66
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:07,200
I found it!

67
00:04:07,370 --> 00:04:09,450
That's so great for you guys!

68
00:04:09,620 --> 00:04:11,120
You must be so happy!

69
00:04:11,290 --> 00:04:14,250
Yes, I am. One of the many things I'm feeling.

70
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:19,960
Good luck with your girlfriend.

71
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:19,960
Oh, thank you. Ah, eh.

72
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,340
Rachel!

73
00:04:28,470 --> 00:04:31,520
You got my message?

74
00:04:28,470 --> 00:04:31,520
You are right on time!

75
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:34,180
So can I be your girlfriend again?

76
00:04:34,350 --> 00:04:35,940
Yes, you can. Very much.

77
00:04:42,190 --> 00:04:44,320
Hey.

78
00:04:42,190 --> 00:04:44,320
Hey.

79
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:48,030
Why are you mopping your ceiling?

80
00:04:44,490 --> 00:04:48,030
Ugh, there's banana on it.

81
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:52,660
I have the spirit of an old Indian woman living in mine.

82
00:04:53,910 --> 00:04:54,960
So then you know.

83
00:04:58,290 --> 00:05:00,540
The mailman was here, so I brought your mail.

84
00:05:00,710 --> 00:05:03,880
Oh, good. Thanks.

85
00:05:00,710 --> 00:05:03,880
Now, what is Fabutech?

86
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:07,180
Okay. Don't judge me too much, okay?

87
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:10,800
I saw this infomercial, and, um, I swear I have never...

88
00:05:10,970 --> 00:05:13,220
...bought anything on TV before.

89
00:05:13,390 --> 00:05:15,230
Except for this mop.

90
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,350
But there was this stuff on leg-waxing, it looked amazing.

91
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:21,230
Waxine!

92
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:21,230
Yes! Have you seen it?

93
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:24,030
It's incredible! I want to be a Waxine Girl!

94
00:05:24,190 --> 00:05:25,440
I know!

95
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:30,280
God! Do you think it really doesn't hurt? How can they do that?

96
00:05:30,450 --> 00:05:33,870
Hello! Organic substances recently discovered in the rain forest?

97
00:05:34,410 --> 00:05:36,790
They have the best stuff in there.

98
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:40,690
Oh, my God!

99
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:42,280
Oh, my God!

100
00:05:43,210 --> 00:05:47,300
We figured when we couldn't find you, you'd gone to make up with Rachel.

101
00:05:47,470 --> 00:05:49,680
Which is probably what you should have done, huh? Heh.

102
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:52,760
You think?

103
00:05:53,770 --> 00:05:57,230
God, I'm in hell. I mean, what am I gonna do?

104
00:05:57,390 --> 00:06:01,560
Rachel's all "I love you," and all I can think about...

105
00:06:01,730 --> 00:06:04,570
...is what is she gonna do when I tell her what I did?

106
00:06:04,730 --> 00:06:08,570
First, we should address the more important question...

107
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:10,160
...how dumb are you?

108
00:06:12,330 --> 00:06:16,240
What? Look, we're trying to rebuild a relationship here, right?

109
00:06:16,410 --> 00:06:19,040
How am I supposed to do that without being honest?

110
00:06:19,210 --> 00:06:22,540
I'm on board about the total-honesty thing. I am.

111
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:26,300
Just not about stuff that's gonna get you in trouble.

112
00:06:26,590 --> 00:06:29,930
He's right. Nobody benefits, and you'll just hurt her.

113
00:06:30,090 --> 00:06:32,890
And there won't be a relationship left to rebuild.

114
00:06:33,050 --> 00:06:34,100
Don't you think...?

115
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:37,810
If you have to tell her, at least wait till the timing's right.

116
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:40,020
And that's what deathbeds are for.

117
00:06:42,980 --> 00:06:44,980
Yeah, okay.

118
00:06:42,980 --> 00:06:44,980
All right.

119
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:50,320
Okay. Now, we just have to make sure she doesn't find out some other way.

120
00:06:51,570 --> 00:06:53,820
Did you think about the trail?

121
00:06:55,870 --> 00:06:57,410
What trail?

122
00:06:59,250 --> 00:07:00,960
From the woman you did it with...

123
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:04,420
...to the woman you hope never finds out you did it!

124
00:07:05,130 --> 00:07:07,090
Always think about the trail!

125
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:11,340
I don't think there's any trail.

126
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:12,970
Okay, okay.

127
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:15,470
Chloe works with that guy, Isaac.

128
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:19,890
Isaac's sister is Jasmine, who works at the massage place with Phoebe.

129
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:23,060
Phoebe is Rachel's friend, and that's the trail! I did it!

130
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:28,900
"After applying the Waxine and linen strips to leg..."

131
00:07:29,070 --> 00:07:30,530
Did that!

132
00:07:29,070 --> 00:07:30,530
Okay.

133
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:33,860
"Grasp the linen strip by its tab...

134
00:07:34,030 --> 00:07:35,410
...and pull it off in one quick...

135
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,700
...pain-free motion."

136
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:37,700
Okay.

137
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:43,040
Was it not "pain-free"?

138
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:46,210
No, it was pain-ful!

139
00:07:46,380 --> 00:07:50,010
My God, they should call it "Pain-zine, now with a little wax."

140
00:07:51,630 --> 00:07:55,510
The girls on the commercial don't seem to think it's that bad.

141
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:58,850
Because their nerves are deadened from being so stupid.

142
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:04,850
But, you know, if you don't believe me, please be my guest.

143
00:08:06,770 --> 00:08:08,980
Ow, ow, ow! Oh, my God!

144
00:08:09,570 --> 00:08:12,610
Now are you glad we didn't start with the bikini strips?

145
00:08:18,410 --> 00:08:19,580
Chloe, hi.

146
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:22,700
Is this about me taking your watch?

147
00:08:23,750 --> 00:08:26,880
You took my watch?

148
00:08:23,750 --> 00:08:26,880
I'm sorry. I do that.

149
00:08:27,750 --> 00:08:31,250
You keep it. Listen, did you tell anyone about us?

150
00:08:31,420 --> 00:08:34,590
Oh, no. I feel like it really isn't anybody's business.

151
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:37,970
Exactly. So you didn't mention anything to Isaac?

152
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:41,890
Oh, I tell Isaac everything.

153
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:41,890
You do? Of course you do.

154
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:47,310
Hi, Isaac. You know, we haven't actually met.

155
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:49,110
You dog!

156
00:08:51,940 --> 00:08:56,400
Yes, I suppose I am a dog. But see, I happen to have a girlfriend.

157
00:08:56,570 --> 00:08:58,820
Right. Rachel from the coffee place.

158
00:08:58,990 --> 00:09:01,870
That's the one. Listen, I don't want to hurt her.

159
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:04,830
Oh, hey, man, I know. It doesn't matter how much we love them.

160
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,540
Monogamy is too cruel a rule.

161
00:09:09,460 --> 00:09:13,880
Yeah. Listen, can you keep this information to yourself?

162
00:09:14,050 --> 00:09:16,630
Oh, no problem. We gotta look out for each other.

163
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:18,550
We're the same, you and me.

164
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:24,270
Actually, no, we're not. Heh.

165
00:09:24,430 --> 00:09:25,850
Yeah, we are.

166
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:28,230
No, we're not.

167
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:29,730
Yeah, we are.

168
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:32,110
No, we're not.

169
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:34,780
Okay, we're not.

170
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:34,780
Right.

171
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:36,320
But we are.

172
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:42,080
Fine. I just need to know that you're not gonna tell your sister.

173
00:09:42,870 --> 00:09:45,160
I can promise not to tell her again.

174
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:50,420
Jasmine?

175
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:53,420
We met at Phoebe's birthday party. I'm Ross Geller.

176
00:09:54,170 --> 00:09:55,920
You did a bad thing!

177
00:09:57,340 --> 00:09:58,840
Yes, I did.

178
00:09:57,340 --> 00:09:58,840
Very bad!

179
00:09:59,010 --> 00:10:00,890
Very bad.

180
00:09:59,010 --> 00:10:00,890
Very, very bad!

181
00:10:01,970 --> 00:10:03,260
I'm agreeing with you.

182
00:10:03,430 --> 00:10:05,930
Listen, did you happen to tell Phoebe yet?

183
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:08,600
No.

184
00:10:06,100 --> 00:10:08,600
Okay. Jasmine.

185
00:10:08,770 --> 00:10:11,270
Please. Please don't.

186
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:15,860
I love my girlfriend very much and I want to work it out with her.

187
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:18,900
All right.

188
00:10:19,570 --> 00:10:21,200
Thank you. Thank you.

189
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:25,290
But you should talk to my roommate. I told him, and he knows Phoebe too.

190
00:10:25,870 --> 00:10:27,000
Who's your roommate?

191
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:29,040
Gunther! Gunther!

192
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:34,920
Tell me you didn't tell Rachel about me and the girl from the copy place.

193
00:10:35,550 --> 00:10:36,880
I'm sorry.

194
00:10:37,050 --> 00:10:38,880
Was I not supposed to?

195
00:10:58,990 --> 00:11:02,200
We're all right.

196
00:10:58,990 --> 00:11:02,200
It's okay. It's okay.

197
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:06,370
Ooh! We were just waxing our legs.

198
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:06,370
Off?

199
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:12,120
For your information, this is a pain like no man will ever experience.

200
00:11:12,290 --> 00:11:15,090
You can't make that statement unless you've been kicked in an area...

201
00:11:15,250 --> 00:11:18,000
...that God only meant to be treated nicely.

202
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:23,050
Women just have a lower threshold for pain than men, that's all.

203
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:25,850
I mean, come on, it's just a little wax. Heh.

204
00:11:26,430 --> 00:11:27,720
Oh, yeah? Come here.

205
00:11:29,850 --> 00:11:31,270
Oh, that's mature.

206
00:11:33,060 --> 00:11:34,940
So now I just pull it off?

207
00:11:35,110 --> 00:11:36,190
That's right.

208
00:11:43,570 --> 00:11:45,780
Rachel, come on. Just talk to me. Please!

209
00:11:45,950 --> 00:11:48,410
I can't look at you right now.

210
00:11:45,950 --> 00:11:48,410
What?

211
00:11:49,370 --> 00:11:51,160
Nothing. Nothing.

212
00:11:51,870 --> 00:11:54,870
She said it was okay.

213
00:11:51,870 --> 00:11:54,870
What are they talking about?

214
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:59,710
Just get away from me!

215
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:59,710
I made a mistake, okay?

216
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:03,930
A mistake? What were you trying to put it in? Her purse?

217
00:12:05,390 --> 00:12:08,430
Whe...? Where did he put it?

218
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:13,810
You had sex with another woman!

219
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,020
Oh, my God!

220
00:12:16,190 --> 00:12:20,690
I knew something was wrong because my nails didn't grow at all yesterday.

221
00:12:22,190 --> 00:12:25,030
I guess they had a fight, and he got drunk...

222
00:12:25,490 --> 00:12:28,120
You guys knew about this and didn't tell us?

223
00:12:28,280 --> 00:12:30,790
He has sex, and we get hit in our heads!

224
00:12:31,370 --> 00:12:33,870
I want you to leave! Get out! Now!

225
00:12:31,370 --> 00:12:33,870
No! No!

226
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:36,000
I want to stay and talk about this.

227
00:12:36,170 --> 00:12:39,130
Okay! All right. How was she?

228
00:12:44,630 --> 00:12:46,260
What?

229
00:12:44,630 --> 00:12:46,260
Was she good?

230
00:12:46,430 --> 00:12:47,510
Don't answer that.

231
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:54,310
You said you wanted to talk about it. Let's talk. How was she?

232
00:12:55,690 --> 00:12:57,190
She was...

233
00:12:55,690 --> 00:12:57,190
Awful.

234
00:12:57,350 --> 00:13:00,480
She was not good.

235
00:12:57,350 --> 00:13:00,480
Horrible. Nothing compared to you.

236
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:03,400
She... She was different.

237
00:13:06,610 --> 00:13:08,110
Good different?

238
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,450
Nobody likes change.

239
00:13:12,580 --> 00:13:15,120
Just stop!

240
00:13:12,580 --> 00:13:15,120
What? Okay! Okay! Okay!

241
00:13:15,830 --> 00:13:17,210
Should we do something?

242
00:13:17,370 --> 00:13:19,540
Yeah. Never cheat on Rachel.

243
00:13:21,750 --> 00:13:25,590
I'm sorry, okay? I'm sorry. I was disgusted with myself...

244
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:27,260
...and this morning I was upset...

245
00:13:27,590 --> 00:13:30,090
...and then I got your message, and I was so happy.

246
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:33,390
And all I wanted was to get her out of my apartment...

247
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:36,560
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa! Wait a minute.

248
00:13:38,150 --> 00:13:40,730
What time did your little friend leave?

249
00:13:44,650 --> 00:13:47,570
Oh, my God. She was there? She was still there?

250
00:13:47,740 --> 00:13:50,870
She was in there when I was in there?

251
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:58,540
Listen, the important thing is, she meant nothing to me.

252
00:13:58,710 --> 00:14:02,340
And yet she was worth jeopardizing our relationship!

253
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,210
I didn't think there was a relationship.

254
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,800
We'd broken up.

255
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,800
We were on a break.

256
00:14:08,970 --> 00:14:12,550
That, for all I knew, could last forever. That is a breakup.

257
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:14,560
You're gonna get out of this on a technicality?

258
00:14:14,720 --> 00:14:17,020
I'm not trying to "get out" of anything.

259
00:14:17,180 --> 00:14:19,060
I thought our relationship was dead.

260
00:14:19,230 --> 00:14:23,190
Well, you sure had a hell of a time at the wake.

261
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:27,110
I don't think we should listen to this anymore.

262
00:14:27,280 --> 00:14:29,320
What are you doing? We can't go out.

263
00:14:29,490 --> 00:14:31,780
Why not? I'm hungry.

264
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:35,290
Because they'll know we've been listening.

265
00:14:35,450 --> 00:14:38,290
God! And to have to hear about it from Gunther!

266
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:43,130
Come on, I ran all over the place trying to make sure that didn't happen!

267
00:14:45,250 --> 00:14:47,340
Oh, that is so sweet.

268
00:14:49,010 --> 00:14:51,840
I think I'm falling in love with you all over again.

269
00:14:54,220 --> 00:14:57,640
We can go out. They have other things to worry about.

270
00:14:57,810 --> 00:14:59,020
We'll be fine.

271
00:14:59,180 --> 00:15:02,690
Rachel, I wanted to tell you. I thought I should.

272
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:06,570
And then Chandler and Joey convinced me not to!

273
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:12,910
Wax the door shut. We're never leaving.

274
00:15:14,450 --> 00:15:18,290
It's Phoebe. Someone has to take my 9:00 with Mr. Rehak...

275
00:15:18,450 --> 00:15:21,540
...because it's 9: 15 now, and I'm not there.

276
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:26,880
None of this would've happened if I didn't think...

277
00:15:27,050 --> 00:15:29,420
...you were having sex with Mark.

278
00:15:29,590 --> 00:15:30,720
All right.

279
00:15:31,470 --> 00:15:35,930
Let's say I had slept with Mark. Would you have been able to forgive me?

280
00:15:38,470 --> 00:15:40,180
Yes, I would.

281
00:15:42,690 --> 00:15:47,070
You'd be okay if Mark had kissed me and been naked with me...

282
00:15:47,230 --> 00:15:48,690
...and made love to me?

283
00:15:50,110 --> 00:15:51,280
Yes.

284
00:15:52,490 --> 00:15:56,240
If you knew that our hot, sweaty, writhing bodies were...

285
00:16:00,870 --> 00:16:04,580
Okay. Okay, yeah. I would have been devastated...

286
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:07,420
...but I would still want to be with you.

287
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:10,420
Because, I mean, it's you.

288
00:16:19,850 --> 00:16:21,270
What?

289
00:16:22,140 --> 00:16:24,810
Come on, tell me what you're thinking.

290
00:16:27,560 --> 00:16:29,320
I'm thinking...

291
00:16:32,070 --> 00:16:33,990
...I'm gonna order a pizza.

292
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:38,910
Order a pizza, like...

293
00:16:39,950 --> 00:16:41,700
..."I forgive you"?

294
00:16:46,920 --> 00:16:48,420
Oh, man!

295
00:16:48,590 --> 00:16:50,210
Pizza?

296
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:52,760
I like pizza.

297
00:16:54,050 --> 00:16:56,260
Put olives on the pizza.

298
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:03,600
We could eat the wax! It's organic!

299
00:17:04,810 --> 00:17:07,020
Oh, great. Food with hair on it.

300
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:10,650
No, not the used wax.

301
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:13,150
Because that would be crazy?

302
00:17:16,110 --> 00:17:19,990
Could I get in on that? Because I'm kind of hungry myself.

303
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:21,330
Fine.

304
00:17:21,490 --> 00:17:24,290
Yes, I'd like to order a large pizza.

305
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:27,670
No anchovies.

306
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:27,670
With, uh, extra anchovies.

307
00:17:28,630 --> 00:17:30,080
That's okay. I'll pick them off.

308
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:33,630
And could you chop some up and put it right in the sauce?

309
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:42,470
You can have the last piece if you want.

310
00:17:42,640 --> 00:17:45,480
Well, I should think so. You slept with someone.

311
00:17:58,070 --> 00:18:00,700
They're gonna get through this, aren't they?

312
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:03,870
Yeah. Come on, it's Ross and Rachel.

313
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:05,080
They've got to.

314
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:08,410
What if they don't?

315
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:15,130
You think I need a new walk?

316
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:19,380
What?

317
00:18:19,550 --> 00:18:23,430
Well, I've been walking the same way since high school.

318
00:18:23,850 --> 00:18:27,680
You know how some guys walk into a room and everybody takes notice?

319
00:18:27,850 --> 00:18:29,890
I think I need a take-notice walk.

320
00:18:30,850 --> 00:18:32,940
Are you actually saying these words?

321
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:40,360
What, now you're not even talking to me?

322
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:47,500
Look, Rachel, I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I was out of my mind.

323
00:18:47,870 --> 00:18:49,250
I thought I'd lost you.

324
00:18:49,410 --> 00:18:52,540
How insane must I have been to do something like this?

325
00:18:52,710 --> 00:18:56,800
I don't cheat, right? That's not me. I'm not Joey!

326
00:19:01,090 --> 00:19:02,430
Yeah, okay.

327
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,010
Hey.

328
00:19:07,180 --> 00:19:10,770
It's 3 a.m. They don't know that I've come home yet.

329
00:19:10,940 --> 00:19:13,900
You notice how they aren't wondering where I am?

330
00:19:14,730 --> 00:19:18,070
You know, people can be so self-involved.

331
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:23,490
You know what? I'm not the one that wanted that break.

332
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:26,280
You're the one that bailed. You're the one...

333
00:19:26,450 --> 00:19:28,700
...that ran the moment things got rough.

334
00:19:28,870 --> 00:19:30,080
That's...

335
00:19:28,870 --> 00:19:30,080
That's what?

336
00:19:30,250 --> 00:19:32,920
That is neither here nor there.

337
00:19:30,250 --> 00:19:32,920
Here we are...

338
00:19:33,080 --> 00:19:35,250
...in a spot again. What do you want?

339
00:19:35,420 --> 00:19:39,170
How do you want to handle it? You want to fight for us or bail?

340
00:19:42,470 --> 00:19:44,260
Look, I...

341
00:19:45,050 --> 00:19:49,140
I did a terrible, stupid, stupid thing, okay?

342
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:53,190
I'm sorry. I wish I could take it back, but I can't.

343
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:57,650
I just can't see us throwing away something we know is so damn good.

344
00:19:58,690 --> 00:20:00,820
I love you so much.

345
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:13,370
No, Ross! Don't!

346
00:20:13,540 --> 00:20:16,960
You can't just kiss me and make it all go away.

347
00:20:17,130 --> 00:20:19,500
It doesn't work that way. It doesn't just make it better.

348
00:20:19,670 --> 00:20:21,380
Okay?

349
00:20:19,670 --> 00:20:21,380
Okay, okay.

350
00:20:26,010 --> 00:20:28,050
I think you should go.

351
00:20:29,560 --> 00:20:31,100
What?

352
00:20:31,270 --> 00:20:33,810
I really think you need to go now.

353
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:37,520
Okay. Okay.

354
00:20:38,980 --> 00:20:42,320
This morning you said there was nothing we couldn't work past it.

355
00:20:42,490 --> 00:20:44,200
What the hell did I know?

356
00:20:44,360 --> 00:20:47,410
There's got to be a way we can work past this. Okay?

357
00:20:47,570 --> 00:20:50,580
I can't imagine my life without you.

358
00:20:50,740 --> 00:20:52,290
You know? Without...

359
00:20:54,790 --> 00:20:55,960
Without these arms...

360
00:20:57,080 --> 00:20:59,710
...and your face and heart...

361
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:02,000
...your good heart, Rach, and...

362
00:21:06,510 --> 00:21:07,930
No.

363
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:11,850
I can't. You're a totally different person to me now.

364
00:21:12,520 --> 00:21:17,690
I used to think of you as somebody that would never, ever hurt me.

365
00:21:17,850 --> 00:21:19,020
Ever.

366
00:21:20,650 --> 00:21:22,900
Now I can't stop picturing you with her.

367
00:21:23,070 --> 00:21:26,860
I can't. It doesn't matter what you say or what you do.

368
00:21:27,030 --> 00:21:29,660
It's just changed everything.

369
00:21:32,120 --> 00:21:33,740
Forever.

370
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:46,220
This can't be it.

371
00:21:51,600 --> 00:21:53,760
Then how come it is?

372
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:07,070
They've been quiet for a long time.

373
00:22:08,530 --> 00:22:09,660
Maybe she killed him.

374
00:22:13,910 --> 00:22:15,200
Let's go.

375
00:22:43,110 --> 00:22:44,900
Is that your new walk?

376
00:22:49,400 --> 00:22:51,360
No. I really have to pee.

